+           "_key": "dc8f21271531",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [],
+           "text": "Nestled by the fertile banks of the Nile Delta, the modern silhouette of Cairo was sketched in 969 CE by the visionary Fatimid dynasty. Yet, the land on which today’s city flourishes whispers tales of ancient capitals, their legacy etched in the stones of "
+         },
+         {
+           "_key": "ce5f22e439af",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [
+             "d2b120a3627e"
+           ],
+           "text": "Old Cairo."
+         }
+       ],
+       "markDefs": [
+         {
+           "_key": "d2b120a3627e",
+           "_pendingInternalRef": {
+             "sourceLocale": "en",
+             "wpUrl": "http://travel2egypt.org/private-tour-the-grand-old-cairo-tour/"
+           },
+           "_type": "externalLink",
+           "href": "http://travel2egypt.org/private-tour-the-grand-old-cairo-tour/",
+           "newTab": false
+         }
+       ],
+       "style": "normal"
+     },
+     {
+       "_key": "9c93644715a3",
+       "_type": "block",
+       "children": [
+         {
+           "_key": "a83e0c4de59d",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [],
+           "text": "Cairo has forever pulsed as the heart of political and cultural vibrancy in the region, earning the moniker “the city of a thousand minarets” due to its rich tapestry of Islamic architecture. This city is a recognized World City, proudly bearing a “Beta +” classification from the Globalization and World Cities Research Network (GaWC)."
+         }
+       ],
+       "markDefs": [],
+       "style": "normal"
+     },
+     {
+       "_key": "79b28b9b7368",
+       "_type": "block",
+       "children": [
+         {
+           "_key": "89c15a602ee5",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [],
+           "text": "Home to over 19 million souls across 3,085 square kilometers, Cairo’s expanse outstrips any other Egyptian city. Its urban sprawl is further augmented by an additional 9.5 million residents living in its vicinity. Yet, amidst its grandeur, Cairo faces the challenges of pollution and congestion, akin to other global megacities."
+         }
+       ],
+       "markDefs": [],
+       "style": "normal"
+     },
+     {
+       "_key": "eadca3364e9a",
+       "_type": "block",
+       "children": [
+         {
+           "_key": "698b4f9b6e4e",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [],
+           "text": "The Cairo metro system, one of only two in Africa (alongside Algiers, Algeria), is among the world’s busiest, serving over 4 million passengers annually. Economically, Cairo has led the Middle East since 2005 and ranked 43rd globally on Foreign Policy’s 2010 Global Cities Index."
+         }
+       ],
+       "markDefs": [],
+       "style": "normal"
+     },
+     {
+       "_key": "48cc227cfbe2",
+       "_type": "block",
+       "children": [
+         {
+           "_key": "d34553c79b9d",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [],
+           "text": "Etymology and the Essence of Cairo"
+         }
+       ],
+       "markDefs": [],
+       "style": "h2"
+     },
+     {
+       "_key": "c38b699ca846",
+       "_type": "block",
+       "children": [
+         {
+           "_key": "9d23055f1a69",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [],
+           "text": "Locally referred to as Maṣr, mirroring the Egyptian Arabic term for Egypt, Cairo’s name underscores its integral role within the nation. Its official name, al-Qāhirah, translates to “the Vanquisher” or “the Conqueror,” a nod to the celestial alignment of Mars, known as “the Conquering Star,” during the city’s foundation. This name also celebrates the arrival of Fatimid Caliph Al-Mu’izz, who established Cairo as a capital upon his arrival from Mahdia. The ancient city of Heliopolis, now the suburb of Ain Shams (“Eye of the Sun”), marks another historical layer of this multifaceted city."
+         }
+       ],
+       "markDefs": [],
+       "style": "normal"
+     },
+     {
+       "_key": "89e0f4f61e90",
+       "_type": "block",
+       "children": [
+         {
+           "_key": "0ad6e3804e39",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [],
+           "text": "Cairo’s skyline, dotted with the “thousand minarets,” offers a panorama of attractions captivating visitors worldwide. Highlights include the awe-inspiring "
+         },
+         {
+           "_key": "fbd4b6b7c645",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [
+             "3785f833dc8b"
+           ],
+           "text": "Pyramids of Giza"
+         },
+         {
+           "_key": "7936cb1b5ec9",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [],
+           "text": ", the treasure trove of the Egyptian Museum of Antiquities, the architectural marvel of the Step Pyramids at Saqqara, and the historic Citadel of Saladin. The city’s religious heritage is magnificently displayed at the Mosque of Mohamed Ali and the "
+         },
+         {
+           "_key": "978836c223cd",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [
+             "5d2f677ff9c7"
+           ],
+           "text": "Mosque of Amr"
+         },
+         {
+           "_key": "fbb8e92217ab",
+           "_type": "span",
+           "marks": [],
+           "text": " Ibn El Aas, the first mosque built in Africa."
+         }
+       ],
+       "markDefs": [
+         {
+           "_key": "3785f833dc8b",
+           "_pendingInternalRef": {
+             "sourceLocale": "en",
+             "wpUrl": "http://travel2egypt.org/pyramids-of-giza-sphinx-egyptian-museum-khan-el-khalili-tour/"
+           },
+           "_type": "externalLink",
+           "href": "http://travel2egypt.org/pyramids-of-giza-sphinx-egyptian-museum-khan-el-khalili-tour/",
+           "newTab": false
+         },
+         {
+           "_key": "5d2f677ff9c7",
+           "_pendingInternalRef": {
+             "sourceLocale": "en",
+             "wpUrl": "https://travel2egypt.org/cairo-travel-guide/the-mosque-of-amr-ibn-al-as/"
+           },
